# Build directories
#
# Everything CMake generates lives in one of these. Nothing in a build directory is
# ever worth committing: it is all reproducible from the sources plus the configure
# flags, and the flags themselves are recorded in scripts/ and docs/.
build/
build-*/
examples/build*/
cmake-build-*/
out/

# Generated reference data
#
# ~28 MiB of float64 golden files, reproducible in about a second:
#     python3 tools/gen_reference.py
# Committing them would mean every regeneration shows up as an unreviewable binary
# diff, and a stale golden file is worse than a missing one -- a missing one makes the
# tests skip with an instruction, a stale one makes them fail for the wrong reason.
tests/golden/

# Benchmark run logs
#
# scripts/gpu-run.sh writes a timestamped log here on every run. Numbers that matter
# get pasted into docs/lab-notebook.md by hand -- deliberately, so that a number
# entering the permanent record is a decision rather than a side effect of running a
# script.
runs/

# Model weights
#
# Model files are hundreds of MiB to several GiB. GitHub rejects anything over 100 MiB
# and a repository that once contained a 4 GiB file stays 4 GiB forever, because git
# history is immutable. Keep weights outside the repo or under models/.
models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# Profiler output
#
# Nsight Systems and Nsight Compute reports. Frequently larger than the whole source
# tree. The conclusions belong in the lab notebook; the raw capture does not.
*.nsys-rep
*.ncu-rep
*.qdrep
*.qdstrm
*.nvvp
*.sqlite

# Editor and IDE state
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.vcxproj*
.cache/
compile_commands.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Compiled artifacts that escaped a build directory
#
# They should never appear at the top level, but an in-source `cmake .` or a stray
# manual `g++` invocation puts them there, and an accidentally committed .obj is
# tedious to notice.
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp

# OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
